    {
      "path": "server memory",
      "summary": "Show memory use, page life expectancy and top memory clerks",
      "description": "Two sets. memory, one row: physical_mb and available_os_mb (sys.dm_os_sys_memory), max_server_memory_mb and min_server_memory_mb (the running values, sys.configurations' value_in_use), committed_mb and target_mb (Memory Manager's Total and Target Server Memory), page_life_expectancy_s (Buffer Manager's, instance-wide) and memory_grants_pending (Memory Manager's); a counter the server does not publish is null. clerks: the 10 memory clerk types holding the most (sys.dm_os_memory_clerks, summed over NUMA nodes), largest first. Every figure but min/max is a DMV, so without VIEW SERVER STATE (VIEW SERVER PERFORMANCE STATE from SQL Server 2022) the command fails, exit 9. Warnings, facts only: max server memory at its default (unlimited); available OS memory under 5 % of physical; memory grants pending.",
