    {
      "path": "server config get",
      "summary": "Show settings by name or alias, with the CPU or memory context to judge them",
      "description": "The list's row for each setting named, in the order given. A name is an alias (maxdop, cost-threshold, max-memory, min-memory, adhoc, backup-compression, backup-checksum, remote-dac, clr, xp-cmdshell, contained-auth, blocked-threshold) or a full sys.configurations name, ignoring case; an unknown one is exit 8 naming up to 3 that contain it. default is the engine's own default on this major version (gosmo's table, from Microsoft's sp_configure reference), not what Setup or mssql-conf writes (Setup recommends MAXDOP and max server memory); it is null where gosmo has none (an option a CU added, Azure), with a warning naming them. The record beside the set is context: logicalCpus, numaNodes and logicalCpusPerNumaNode for max degree of parallelism and cost threshold for parallelism; physicalMemoryMb and committedMemoryMb (Total Server Memory) for max and min server memory. They need VIEW SERVER STATE (VIEW SERVER PERFORMANCE STATE from SQL Server 2022): without it they are null with one warning (exit 0).",
