    {
      "path": "server config set",
      "summary": "Change sp_configure settings in one batch; before/after and restarts",
      "description": "Takes name value pairs; a name is as for server config get, and a negative value follows --. Needs --allow admin. Every change runs in one gosmo ApplyConfiguration batch: show advanced options turned on only if an advanced option needs it and put back after, each sp_configure, one RECONFIGURE (WITH OVERRIDE under --override, for values the plain form refuses). --dry-run prints that batch and a planned_change set (current, new, and enables_show_advanced: whether its first step fires here) without running it. Otherwise the change set holds before, requested, after_configured and after_running, read back from sys.configurations, and restart_required (the running value is not the configured one; min server memory 0, which runs as 16, aside). A batch the server failed exits 5 with the change set still read back: an sp_configure it refused leaves its row unchanged, and a refused RECONFIGURE leaves every change configured but not running, pending until the next RECONFIGURE (the hint says so). Blocked (exit 7) unless --accept-risk: max or min server memory above physical memory, max below min server memory, max degree of parallelism above the logical CPUs, and any of these when the login cannot read the figure (VIEW SERVER STATE); a value that is the option's default is never risky. Warnings: a new max server memory below committed memory, and a value that waits for a restart. A value is a whole number in the setting's own unit; an option whose name ends in (MB) also takes an MB, GB or TB suffix, one ending in (KB) a KB or MB suffix, ignoring case, as long as the result is whole in that unit (1.5GB = 1536). A value outside the option's min and max (its default aside: 0 for the self-configuring ones), a unit on another option or a setting named twice is exit 2, before anything runs.",
      "operationClass": "admin",
      "arguments": [
        {
          "name": "name",
          "help": "A setting's alias or sys.configurations name",
          "format": null,
          "required": true,
          "repeat": false
        },
        {
          "name": "value",
          "help": "Its new value; further name value pairs may follow",
          "format": null,
          "required": true,
          "repeat": true
        }
      ],
      "options": [
        {
