    {
      "path": "db files",
      "summary": "List a database's files: size, space used and free, autogrowth, max size, free space on the volume",
      "description": "One row per file, data and log alike, read inside the database (sys.database_files and FILEPROPERTY), so tempdb's sizes are its current ones. --all reports every database, system ones included, with a database column first. A database that cannot be read inside (not ONLINE, or no user for the login) is listed from sys.master_files with filegroup, used, free and free_pct NULL and a warning saying why. A FILESTREAM or full-text container has no pages: its used, free, free_pct, growth and max_size are NULL. max_size reads unlimited, or a size in the unit; growth reads as a percentage, none, or a size in KB under --unit kb and in MB otherwise. volume_free_pct is the free space on the volume holding the file (sys.dm_os_volume_stats, which needs VIEW SERVER STATE; NULL with a warning without it). A snapshot lists its own sparse files, whose size is a ceiling. used is NULL where FILEPROPERTY answers nothing (the login cannot see the file). --max-free-pct keeps files whose free_pct is known and at most the figure, compared exactly rather than on the rounded text. --sort-by: name (database, then logical name), size and used largest first, free-pct fullest first; NULLs last. Without it, files are in database, then file_id order. Warnings, for the rows shown only: a data or log file under 10 % free inside it, at 90 % or more of a capped max_size, or growing by a percentage (not a snapshot's, which never grows); a file on a volume under 10 % free; a snapshot's file, whose size is a ceiling, with the space it occupies on disk.",
