    {
      "path": "db space",
      "summary": "Show a database's space summary as sp_spaceused reports it, with its log usage",
      "description": "One row per database, read inside it: total (sp_spaceused's database_size: data and log files, and from SQL Server 2017 the memory-optimized checkpoint files), data_size and data_used (the data files and the space allocated in them), unallocated, reserved, data, index and unused, all in sp_spaceused's arithmetic so they match its output exactly. log_size, log_used and log_used_pct are sys.dm_db_log_space_usage's, the DMV's own figures; it needs VIEW SERVER STATE (VIEW SERVER PERFORMANCE STATE from SQL Server 2022), and without it they are NULL with one warning. log_size is the log's usable size, a little under the log files' size. --all reports every database, system ones included; one that cannot be read inside (not ONLINE, or no user for the login) is named under warnings instead. A named one that cannot be read fails: exit 8 for its state, 9 for the login's access. A snapshot's figures are its source's as of the snapshot's creation, as sp_spaceused reports them there; it has no log, so its log columns are NULL, with a warning.",
