    {
      "path": "db log-usage",
      "summary": "Show a database's transaction log usage, why it cannot be truncated, and its VLFs",
      "description": "One row per database, read inside it: log_size, log_used and log_used_pct are sys.dm_db_log_space_usage's, the DMV's own figures, as db space shows them; log_size is the log's usable size, a little under the log files' size. log_reuse_wait_desc is sys.databases', what the log waits on before its space can be reused. vlf_count and vlf_active count sys.dm_db_log_info's virtual log files, all and active ones; the DMV exists from SQL Server 2016 SP2 (13.0.5026), and on an older build both are NULL with a warning. Both DMVs need VIEW SERVER STATE (VIEW SERVER PERFORMANCE STATE from SQL Server 2022): without it the command fails, exit 9. --all reports every database, system ones included, except snapshots, which have no log; one that cannot be read inside (not ONLINE, or no user for the login) is named under warnings instead. A named one that cannot be read fails: exit 8 for its state or a snapshot, 9 for the login's access. Warnings: a log whose reuse waits on anything but NOTHING, transient waits such as CHECKPOINT included.",
      "operationClass": "read",
      "arguments": [
        {
          "name": "name",
          "help": "Database name; or --all",
          "format": null,
          "required": false,
          "repeat": false
        }
      ],
      "options": [
        {
          "name": "--profile",
          "short": "-p",
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [],
          "default": null,
          "negation": null,
          "env": "GOSSMS_PROFILE",
          "help": "Saved connection profile (gossms profile list); connection options override its values"
        },
        {
          "name": "--server",
          "short": "-S",
          "type": "string",
