    {
      "path": "db scoped-config set",
      "summary": "Change one database scoped configuration, for the primary or readable secondaries",
      "description": "ALTER DATABASE SCOPED CONFIGURATION, run inside the database. Needs --allow admin, and ALTER ANY DATABASE SCOPED CONFIGURATION in the database (without it: exit 9). The name is as for get. The value is checked against the configuration's type before anything runs (exit 2): a switch takes ON or OFF (1 and 0 are sent as ON and OFF: the statement refuses a number there), a number a whole number of 0 or more, a keyword a word of letters, digits and _; a quoted value (a URL) is not supported here. --for-secondary sets the value readable secondaries use (FOR SECONDARY), and PRIMARY, only there, makes them follow the primary again; the server accepts it for a database in no availability group too, and refuses it for a configuration that has no secondary value. --dry-run prints the statement and a planned_change set (name, replica, current, new) without running it. Otherwise the change set holds before, requested and after, from the view read before and after. Both sets spell values as the statement does: ON or OFF for a switch, PRIMARY for a secondary value that follows the primary.",
