    {
      "path": "object dependencies",
      "summary": "Show what an object uses and what uses it, as View Dependencies does",
      "description": "One row per dependency edge. uses: the objects <object>'s own definition references (tables, views, functions, procedures it calls); used-by: the objects whose definition references <object>. --depth n follows the edges n levels out: level 1 is <object>'s own, level 2 those of the objects at level 1, and so on; via names the object at the level before. An object reached twice is followed once, so a cycle ends. Only objects in the connection's database are listed: a reference to another database, or to an object that does not exist, is not. schema_bound marks a WITH SCHEMABINDING reference; caller_dependent a one-part name resolved, as the module's owner would, against its schema and then dbo — another caller may get a different object.",
