      "path": "plan actual",
      "summary": "Run T-SQL and show its actual execution plan (SET STATISTICS XML ON)",
      "description": "Runs the script as query run does — the same --allow check and ceiling, --transaction, --max-rows-affected, --param, stop on the first failing batch unless --continue-on-error, --timeout, --dry-run — under SET STATISTICS XML ON, and answers each executed statement's plan with its actual rows, executions and times. The script really runs: a write needs --allow write, and --transaction rollback measures it without keeping the change. Its rows are counted, not returned: set result_sets has each set's columns and row count (query run returns the rows). The login needs SHOWPLAN in the database (exit 9 without it). SET STATISTICS XML in the script is refused (exit 7), as are SET PARSEONLY, NOEXEC and SHOWPLAN_* ON. --plan-format, --top and --plan-file as for plan estimated; the summary's actual columns (actual_rows, elapsed_ms, cpu_ms, misestimate) are filled. A failed or timed-out run still answers the plans the server sent before it stopped; a batch cut by --timeout loses its own, which the server had not yet sent.",
