    {
      "path": "data top",
      "summary": "Select the first rows of a table or view (Select Top N Rows)",
      "description": "SELECT TOP (--rows) of the object, as Object Explorer's Select Top 1000 Rows, with every column (*) unless --columns names some. --columns is a comma-separated list of column names, bracketed where a name needs it ([Order Date]); each is checked against the object's columns (exit 8 naming close matches), never spliced as written. Without --order-by the order is whatever the server returns. A record — object, type, tsql (the SELECT sent) — then the rows; --max-rows still cuts what stdout shows, so --rows above it needs --max-rows 0 or --out-file.",
