    {
      "path": "data export",
      "summary": "Write every row of a table, a view or a read query to a file",
      "description": "Streams every row — no row, width or byte limit — to --out-file, which is required; its extension names the format as for any command: .csv and .tsv (the TUI's Results To File writer: NULL an empty field, the empty string \"\", the same bytes for the same rows), .jsonl (typed rows, then the summary), .json, .md, .txt. The file is replaced only when the export succeeds, and an existing one needs --force. Give an object — SELECT * of it, with --columns, --where and --order-by as data top's (the composed statement must stay one SELECT, else BLOCKED, exit 7) — or the T-SQL in exactly one of --sql, --file or --sql-base64, which runs as query run does with the class fixed at read: anything above read is BLOCKED (exit 7) before connecting, and the run stops at the first failing batch. Every result set goes to the file. stdout gets the record — object, type, tsql; or detectedClass and statementCount — with each set's row count and outFile.",
